Description: headless GNOME desktop streamed to a web browser
 Gives an existing account on an existing machine a full GNOME desktop that is
 reachable from a browser, without containers and without a graphics card. A
 systemd template unit starts an X server on the dummy driver, a GNOME session
 and the Selkies streaming server, one instance per session.
 .
 Each session is allocated a port from a fixed block, so a reverse proxy in
 front of the machine can be configured once from a predictable mapping. The
 whole block is covered by the package's own nftables table, which restricts
 which addresses may reach it. A session starts when somebody first connects,
 rather than at boot, and is stopped again after a configurable idle period.
 .
 A session may optionally be isolated from any other desktop belonging to the
 same account, which allows a browser session to coexist with a desktop that is
 already logged in against the same shared home directory.
